 "▼ Dive in: <0>Comparison</0>": "",
 "<0>MCP</0> (Model Context Protocol) standardises how an agent app connects to <1>tools and data</1> servers: discover tools, call them, read resources.": "",
 "<0>A2A</0> (agent-to-agent) protocols aim to let <1>agents talk to other agents</1> across vendors/frameworks; the space is young and still shifting.": "",
 "<0>Skills</0> are packaged instructions (plus files/scripts) loaded on demand: they change <1>what the model knows how to do</1>, not what it can connect to.": "",
 "All three end up as <0>text in the context</0>: tool schemas, tool results, skill instructions. None of them changes the model weights.": "",
 "MCP messages use JSON-RPC {#}; check the current spec for transports, auth and versions.": "",
